course: dictionary
lesson: 6525
title: Nervous: worry, bodies and brains
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nervous is an adjective. It usually means feeling worried or a little scared about something that is going to happen, like a test or a show. «Confident speakers still feel nervous; practising, breathing slowly and starting with a smile help.» So even confident people can feel nervous, and that is normal.
explain: A nervous person or animal is easily frightened or upset. You can say someone is nervous about something or nervous of something, and you can feel nervous. Look for these clues in a text: a character who keeps checking the door, or a dog that will not come near strangers.
explain: The word nervous also belongs to science. The nervous system is the brain, spinal cord and nerves that carry messages around the body. It lets you feel, think and move. This is a different meaning, so check the context to see which one the writer means.
fact: Nervous means feeling worried or a little scared about something that is going to happen.
fact: Nervous can also describe a person or animal who is easily frightened or upset.
fact: Nervous can be used with about, as in nervous about, or of, as in nervous of.
fact: The nervous system is the brain, spinal cord and nerves that carry messages around the body.
fact: Nervous is an adjective, and its comparisons are more nervous and most nervous.
exercise: «Confident speakers still feel nervous; practising and breathing slowly help.» What does nervous mean here? | Very happy and relaxed | Sleepy after a long day | *Worried or a little scared about speaking | Loud and bossy
exercise: What is the nervous system? | A set of stairs in a school | *The brain, spinal cord and nerves that carry messages around the body | The food you eat each day | The bones that hold up the body
exercise: Vibrato is «a controlled wobble in the voice that singers use on purpose, different from a nervous shake.» Why is vibrato different from a nervous shake? | *Singers use it on purpose | It is caused by being scared | It makes the voice go quiet | It happens only to dogs
test: «Feeling nervous is normal; you can tell the dentist, ask what they will do, and agree a signal.» Which action does the sentence suggest to help with nervous feelings? | Hide from the dentist | Refuse to go to the dentist ever again | *Tell the dentist how you feel and ask what they will do | Shout at the dentist
test: Which sign of being nervous is in the sentence «a dog may wag because it is nervous»? | A loud purr | *A wagging tail | A long sleep | A bright, shiny coat
exam: «Zara went red and felt a bit nervous, but her eyes were fine.» What does nervous mean in this sentence? | Easily frightened or upset, or feeling worried about the eye check | Very cheerful and loud | Part of the brain that makes you tired | *Feeling worried or a little scared about something that is going to happen
